; Fixed Gamma text uses ordinary character literals, grouped eight at a time.
; Balanced addition sequences writes left to right without pairs or per-chunk
; bindings. Each leaf returns a byte or a sum of eight bytes; the largest body
; writes 660 bytes, so every sum is nonnegative and at most 660 * 255.
; Counting advances once without evaluating any writer; publication keeps
; the same fixed extent. Exact emitted text is pinned by the staged gate.
(def emit_eight_bytes ((first Int) (second Int) (third Int) (fourth Int) (fifth Int) (sixth Int) (seventh Int) (eighth Int)) Int
  (+ (+ (+ (write first)
    (write second))
    (+ (write third)
    (write fourth)))
    (+ (+ (write fifth)
    (write sixth))
    (+ (write seventh)
    (write eighth)))))

